{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/978735-so-i-ve-been-reading-the-infinite-tapestry","id":978735,"title":"So, I've been reading The Infinite Tapestry...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-29T17:33:45-07:00","id":978735,"title":"So, I've been reading The Infinite Tapestry...","content":"...and wow is this thing oblique!<br /> <br /> I have myself a copy of the Book of Worlds, and I've been trying to read and skim through both in order to get a clear idea of, more or less, how the umbra functions. (I've also been reading a few Werewolf books. No Wraith though, can't find any PDFs for Wraith anywhere, and Wr20 looks like a pretty long wait).<br /> <br /> I'm aware that M20 pretty much said &quot;Hey, The Umbra's weird, go nuts with it!&quot; and that's great and all, but it doesn't really help when it comes to grasping concepts.<br /> I know that Tapestry focuses on the High Umbra in incredible detail, so I've been a bit reluctant to read what Worlds has to say about it in case of mind melting contradictions. Though skimming through the Outer World's sections in both books, I get the impression that Worlds goes into way more detail on Shard realms and Horizon realms, while Tapestry only really &quot;updates&quot; them for Revised's metaplot, while kinda assuming you already know what's there. So, is this also the case for the High Umbra?<br /> <br /> That and Tapestry seems to hand wave the Middle and Lower Umbra entirely, saying &quot;read Werewolf&quot; for the former and &quot;That place is GONE&quot; for the latter. And the Maya is just completely ignored. Making this book much less useful for understanding the Umbra than I hoped it would be.<br /> <br /> - So, here's my question. When running an Umbra game, how much do you dip into Worlds vs Tapestry for your games these days?<br /> - What are your thoughts on the High Umbra of Tapestry? What kind of Umbrood Courts and Spires have you used or thought up for your games?<br /> - For the middle umbra, what kind of environment do you create for the spaces between realms? Full on wilderness? Do you put expansive planes, prairies, deserts and wastelands in between, or is it more a case of wondering around from realm to realm?<br /> - Are there other sources you recommend I read to get a better handle of this inherently disorienting area?<br /> <br /> Just before you get into this, I know the Umbra only really has a vague form of internal consistency, and that technically everything can be canon at once. This isn't what I'm worried about. My personal mage world is one where the Avatar Storm exists but so does the Lower Umbra (it just came back into being because...umbra?), so I'm quite familiar with ignoring &quot;official&quot; Meta-canon for the sake of keeping what one prefers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T01:24:11-07:00","id":978918,"title":"","content":"Infinite Tapestry is not really a book about Umbra, is a book about Umbral travelling after the Avatar Storm, so its focus is just on the changes the Avatar Storm brought on.<br /> The main source for Umbra remains the Book of the worlds, and in a lesser degree the Book of Madness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T02:22:09-07:00","id":978930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/978735-so-i-ve-been-reading-the-infinite-tapestry?p=978918#post978918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Infinite Tapestry is not really a book about Umbra, is a book about Umbral travelling after the Avatar Storm, so its focus is just on the changes the Avatar Storm brought on.<br /> The main source for Umbra remains the Book of the worlds, and in a lesser degree the Book of Madness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which book of madness? The old one or the revised one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1219